#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105903 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105560 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "62405619-31ca-5403-aa45-360e6b3fbd59" :question/math-academy-id "e-3289" :question/problem "Find the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ below. Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n![](images/dc/dc625408598aa3cbfda44ec877c9a26ab563dee9fcf757192fcf2cf8411f606a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin{C},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{C}$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =CB=58 \\\\ b & =CA=40 \\\\ m∠C & ={31}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\sin{31^{\\circ}} = 0.515\\,038\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 58\\cdot 40\\operatorname{sin}⁡{31}^{∘} \\\\  & =1160\\cdot (0.515\\,038) \\\\  & ≈597.44,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049449}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528224 :question-generator/id #uuid "6a47fdf1-4be6-5b0e-b9be-3377eba83cf9" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186105903.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023bf6fd-e4e6-5fbd-8396-62dfe5c743a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281712} {:answer/id #uuid "67c80e22-6694-51dc-ae09-603484761f48" :answer/type {:db/ide