98b732958447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "93.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293632} :answer-field/id #uuid "d61c4e2c-bb73-58b5-9e0a-477efb52fb86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e614497f-203d-5c49-a415-3fb541b41cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279753" :question/problem "![](images/68/68977537a5f180dd483534ed1415326251d4a76a3dd0833e9701487cd8b5b33d.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{ft}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=18, \\\\ b & =AC=12, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 18\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =108\\cdot (0.866\\,025…) \\\\  & ≈93.5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest tenth**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295123 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e971691-e630-503f-870f-b92b3ea2ce77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e971691-e630-503f-870f-b92b3ea2ce77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.83" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293443} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f6faf19-04cc-502f-9255-547f6f88a2b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8878e119-056d-550e-93df-4c14bd85326c" :question/math-academy-id "q-280260" :question/problem "![](images/20/200dcd87827ae9683ba0ecb3b284509b31d32f9e0dc1b9736a260d2f7d71b0a0.png)\n\nRounded to **two decimal places**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5, \\\\ a & =BC=5, \\\\ m∠B & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=0.866\\,025,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =12.5\\cdot (0.866\\,025) \\\\  & ≈10.83,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to **two decimal places**."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b00af7-b5df-5196-b2de-1c4b578c6353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528150} {:answer/id #uuid "38ff0ae6-d364-5437-aee1-a57108c7d158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528156} {:answer/id #uuid "5e563a3e-30b4-58b1-9d8f-82d50ebca762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528168} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2e8905-558c-5e9d-bec6-bfbcdc9bbd18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43.06" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528173} {:answer/id #uuid "9567582e-dc45-56ac-bc5f-3a111d30a323" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e563a3e-30b4-58b1-9d8f-82d50ebca762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528168} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea4018e3-3df9-5608-859f-36d302fbcc24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "129248be-068c-5fed-a900-5e4f8d0a77cb" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f8a71c2cbb351253304bca516db5b4b7ca7ed745264083f9eb2bbdb918e19cc0.png)\n\nFind the area of $△ABC$. Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The angles of a triangle sum to $180^{\\circ}$. Thus the included angle is\n\n$$\nm∠B=180^{\\circ}-73^{\\circ}-73^{\\circ}=34^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}ac\\operatorname{sin}⁡B,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠B$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=9.28, \\\\ a & =BC=9.28, \\\\ m∠B & ={34}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{34}^{∘}=0.559\\,193,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9.28\\cdot 9.28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{34}^{∘} \\\\  & =43.0592\\cdot (0.559\\,193) \\\\  & ≈24.08,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4b9075-c923-5501-aeee-25e2282c2b5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528149} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5533f8-06f4-5369-b272-76225d4fe8f0" :a